  "notes": "{汲|く}む means to draw or scoop liquid, typically water, from a source.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Takes ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ for the liquid and ⟦から→から：00504_kara⟧ for the source\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{水|みず}→水：02258_mizu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汲|く}む: to draw water\n- ⟦{井戸|いど}→井戸：03977_ido⟧⟦から→から：00504_kara⟧{汲|く}む: to draw from a well\n- ⟦{湯|ゆ}→湯：01740_yu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汲|く}む: to scoop hot water\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汲|く}む: to understand someone's feelings (figurative)\n\nDISTINCTION (homophones):\n- {汲|く}む: to draw/scoop water\n- ⟦{組|く}む→組む：02050_kumu⟧: to put together, cross (arms), team up\n- ⟦{酌|く}む→酌む：02464_kumu⟧: to pour drinks (for someone)\n\nThe figurative use ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汲|く}む or ⟦{意|い}→意：noentry⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汲|く}む means to understand and appreciate someone's feelings or intentions.",
